# SYNOPSIS

```text
protocol todhchai.gpu.device.Context version 1
call capset() -> [UInt8]
call createBlob(id: UInt64, size: UInt64, flags: UInt32)
  throws(GPUError) -> UInt32
call map(resource: UInt32) throws(GPUError) -> Handle
call release(resource: UInt32)
call addSync(counter: Handle) throws(GPUError) -> UInt32
call removeSync(id: UInt32)
call submit(timeline: UInt32, stream: [UInt8], syncs: [SyncValue])
  throws(GPUError)
```

# DESCRIPTION

Protocol `todhchai.gpu.device.Context`, version 1, of library `GPUDeviceIPC`, its messages in the one wire format (wire(6)).

| Method | Kind | Since | Ordinal |
| `capset` | call | 1 | `0x124e123042a65ca8` |
| `createBlob` | call | 1 | `0x63cf8a2e19fe10b7` |
| `map` | call | 1 | `0x35caa72978a6ffd6` |
| `release` | call | 1 | `0x2f3557de2926a63d` |
| `addSync` | call | 1 | `0x45bf3ddc3e01cb94` |
| `removeSync` | call | 1 | `0x591632459cf667e3` |
| `submit` | call | 1 | `0xfbe8d011fe8f2b8` |

: `capset`
  The capset's bytes.
: `createBlob`
  A blob the renderer makes for the context's object `id` (0: shared
  memory), `flags` as virtio-gpu's (1 mappable); its resource id.
: `map`
  A mappable blob as a VMO over the device's memory, its cache policy
  set as the host asks.
: `addSync`
  A counter of the client's to raise for submissions; its id.
: `submit`
  A command stream for the context's renderer; when the work before
  it on `timeline` is done, each sync is raised to its value.

